<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dandin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th–8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dandin was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> writer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-india">South India</a>, probably active around 700, who is associated with the Pallava court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>. He wrote the Kavyadarsha, 'Mirror of Poetry', one of the most influential works of Sanskrit poetics, later adapted in Tamil, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a>, Sinhala and Tibetan, and the prose romance Dashakumaracharita, 'The Adventures of the Ten Princes'.</p></div>
